  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Kenya - Moringa Plantation &amp; processing facility</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">With a DGGF Start-up Loan, Leafs from Kenya BV will be able to set up a Moringa plantation and processing facility in Kenya together with local subsidiaries.Most of the Moringa that is produced there and processed into powder and tea, finds its way through LEAFS from Kenya B.V. in the Netherlands to customers in Europe and America, among others.  Certainly the high quality and organically certified Moringa that Leafs will grow is very popular.The market for Moringa is growing. Europe often follows the trend of the United States and there the use of dietary supplements and use of Moringa in the food and cosmetics market are already very common. Also due to the current Covid19 situation, more vitamins and supplements are taken.In this start-up phase, investments must be made in mother plants (seeds), means of production, processing areas, in the infrastructure and in the recruitment and training of local employees. The expected impact is local employment of approx. 400fte and knowledge exchange by training the staff.</narrative>
  </description>
